# =====================================================================
# Kaveri Academy — environment contract (placeholders only)
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in real values. .env.local is gitignored.
# NEVER commit real keys. VITE_* values ARE exposed to the browser
# bundle: only ever put public-by-design values there.
#
# Full push-notification setup walk-through:
#   docs/push-notifications-setup.md
# =====================================================================
#
# NOTE: real values live in Infisical and are injected at runtime by
# `infisical run` (see the note at the end of this file, and
# docs/infisical-secrets.md). The "copy to .env.local" flow is now only
# the offline fallback — `npm run dev:plain`.

# --- Supabase (required) ---
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=replace_with_supabase_anon_key

# --- Firebase Web Push (FCM) — public-by-design values ---
# Firebase console > Project settings > General > Your apps > Web app.
# These identify the project; they do not authorize anything sensitive.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=replace_with_firebase_web_api_key
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=replace_with_sender_id
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=replace_with_web_app_id

# VAPID key for Web Push — Firebase console > Project settings >
# Cloud Messaging > Web Push certificates. Required for getToken()
# to succeed and register the device in push_subscriptions.
VITE_FCM_VAPID_KEY=replace_with_vapid_public_key

# --- Optional: preview role override for local QA ---
# Lets local QA browse a portal without an account (see
# src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx). NEVER set in production: a production
# build with this set is refused by scripts/check-preview-role.mjs
# (wired into `npm run build`). Local dev is unaffected — `npm run
# dev:plain` does not run that check.
# VITE_PREVIEW_ROLE=student|faculty

# =====================================================================
# SERVER-ONLY SECRETS — never VITE_*, never in the browser bundle.
# Set these as Supabase function secrets (`supabase secrets set ...`)
# or in the Supabase dashboard. See docs/push-notifications-setup.md.
# =====================================================================
# FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON   Full Firebase service-account JSON, one line
#                            (Project settings > Service accounts >
#                            Generate new private key). Consumed by the
#                            notification-push edge function for FCM HTTP v1.
#                            Alternative: store it as Supabase Vault secret
#                            fcm_service_account_json (the function reads
#                            vault when this env var is unset) — see
#                            docs/push-notifications-setup.md Step 4.
# FCM_PROJECT_ID             Fallback when the JSON lacks project_id
#                            (e.g. kaveri-academy).
# MAILER_PROVIDER            resend | log — fail-closed when unset
#                            (notification-mailer edge function).
# RESEND_API_KEY             Only when MAILER_PROVIDER=resend.
# RESEND_FROM                e.g. "Kaveri Academy <noreply@yourdomain.com>"
# LMS_PUBLIC_URL             Absolute link base in email templates
#                            (e.g. https://www.kaveritech.co.in).
# NOTIFICATION_MAILER_TOKEN  Optional override of the vault secret
#                            notification_mailer_token.
# --- Cashfree payments (sandbox/test only in v1) ---
# Set these as Supabase function secrets (`supabase secrets set ...`)
# for the cashfree-payments edge function. NEVER VITE_* — the secret
# must never reach the browser bundle. Test keys come from the
# Cashfree merchant dashboard > Developers > Payment Gateway > API
# Keys (Test Environment). The test secret can be revealed again from
# the key row menu ("View API Key"). Production keys are a separate,
# deliberate step (new env names, prod KYC, domain whitelist) — do
# NOT point CASHFREE_API_BASE_URL at production with TEST keys.
# CASHFREE_TEST_APP_ID       Test App ID (x-client-id).
# CASHFREE_TEST_SECRET_KEY   Test secret key (x-client-secret). Also
#                            the webhook HMAC key.
# CASHFREE_API_VERSION       PG API version, default 2025-01-01.
# CASHFREE_API_BASE_URL      Default https://sandbox.cashfree.com/pg
#                            (production: https://api.cashfree.com/pg).
#
# --- Payments (browser-side config, public-by-design) ---
# VITE_PAYMENT_PROVIDER      Active gateway, default 'cashfree'.
#                            Overridden at runtime by gateway_settings
#                            (Admin → Payment Settings) when the
#                            20261114120000 migration is applied.
# VITE_PAYMENT_CURRENCY      Checkout currency, default 'INR'.
#
# --- Multi-gateway payments (v2: Razorpay, Stripe, PayPal) ---
# Set these as Supabase function secrets for the matching edge
# function (razorpay-payments, stripe-payments, paypal-payments).
# NEVER VITE_* — secrets must never reach the browser bundle.
# Test/live mode is picked per gateway in Admin → Payment Settings
# (gateway_settings.mode); the function reads the matching secret
# names below. Live activation is a separate, deliberate step
# (live keys + live webhook + KYC where required). See
# docs/payments-multi-gateway.md for the per-gateway setup steps.
# RAZORPAY_TEST_KEY_ID       Test Key ID (rzp_test_...).
# RAZORPAY_TEST_KEY_SECRET   Test Key Secret.
# RAZORPAY_TEST_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#                            Webhook secret chosen at webhook
#                            registration (separate from Key Secret).
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID            Live Key ID (mode 'live' only).
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET        Live Key Secret (mode 'live' only).
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET    Live webhook secret (mode 'live' only).
# STRIPE_TEST_SECRET_KEY     Test secret key (sk_test_...).
# STRIPE_TEST_WEBHOOK_SECRET Test endpoint signing secret (whsec_...).
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY          Live secret key (mode 'live' only).
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET      Live endpoint signing secret (mode 'live' only).
# PAYPAL_TEST_CLIENT_ID      Sandbox REST app Client ID.
# PAYPAL_TEST_CLIENT_SECRET  Sandbox REST app Client Secret.
# PAYPAL_TEST_WEBHOOK_ID     Sandbox webhook ID.
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID           Live REST app Client ID (mode 'live' only).
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET       Live REST app Client Secret (mode 'live' only).
# PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID          Live webhook ID (mode 'live' only).
# LMS_PUBLIC_URL             Required by Stripe + PayPal (Checkout
#                            success/cancel and order return URLs).

# =====================================================================
# Infisical is the source of truth for these values — no .env file is
# required to run the app (`npm run dev` wraps the dev server in
# `infisical run --env=dev`; `npm run dev:plain` is the offline fallback).
# Setup guide: docs/infisical-secrets.md
# =====================================================================
